  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Derivative of log and trig function</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p> Find the  derivatives for the following function
<ol>
<li>
<p> \(f(x)={@quest_expr@}\)</p>
<p>\( f'(x) =\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]] </p>
</li>

<li>
<p> \( g(y)= {@quest_exprresion@}\)</p>
<p> \(g'(y)= \) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]] </p>
</li>
</ol>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>
<ol>
<li>
<p>Find the derivatives for the following function.</p>
<p>\(f(x)={@quest_expr@}\)</p>
<p>\(f'(x)={@coef_cos@} \cdot [{@cos(a*x)@}]'+{@coef_sin@} \cdot [{@sin(b*x)@}]'\)</p>
<p>\( f'(x) = {@coef_cos@} \cdot \left[ {@diff(cos(a*x),x)@} \right]+{@coef_sin@} \cdot \left[ {@diff(sin(b*x),x)@} \right] \) </p>
<p>\( f'(x)= \displaystyle {@ta1@}\)</p>
</li>

<li>
<p> Find the derivative for the following function.</p>
<p>\(  g(y)= \displaystyle {@quest_exprresion@}\)</p>
<p> We use the formula \(\displaystyle [\ln(u(y))]'= \displaystyle \frac{u'(y)}{u(y)} \)</p>
<p>Here \(u(y)={@u_y@}\) and \(u'(y)= \displaystyle {@diff(u_y,y)@}\)</p>
<p>Therefore \(g'(y)= \displaystyle {@ta2@} \)</p>
</li>
</ol>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
